es of public policy that might appropriately be pursued to reduce (or increase) inequality. These topics will be addressed in related units, some of which include guest lectures by faculty from other universities (funded by the Center for the Study of Inequality). Each unit culminates with a highly spirited class discussion and debate.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-SBY)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 371056, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "3260", "titleShort": "Building Power from Nothing", "titleLong": "Building Power from Nothing", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17096, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:45PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "bb686", "firstName": "Brittany", "middleName": "M.", "lastName": "Bond"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Ives Hall 215", "bldgDescr": "Ives Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "IVS215", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This is a course about power and influence. We will discuss how to map power and interest patterns in organizations, how to understand various groups' interests and objectives, and how to operate effectively in organizational environments. Organizational actors differ in the power and resources that they bring to bear in order to advance their perspectives. Students will learn how to advance personal interests, even from positions of little structural advantage. This class will develop frameworks as well as a range of practical tools to address these goals. The course will take a macro approach to studying power and influence, focusing on organizational culture, politics, influence, and leadership. Students will learn how to build power from nothing, as well as how to become successful agents of lasting organizational change.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite:\u00a0ILROB 1220.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 370732, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "4295", "titleShort": "Organizations Across Lifecycle", "titleLong": "Organizations Across the Lifecycl